    copy and exports its landing-pad context, which is thread-local in the
    module that defines it but plain data as another module's export, so a
    module whose code throws or catches takes libunwind's own (each module
    unwinds through its own copy, as -Bsymbolic has a library do)."""
    if (nostdlib or nodefaultlibs) and not cxx_rt_named or not os.path.exists(LIB + '/libunwind.a'):
